Antumbra (fork of Shadow)
=========================

This repository is a modified fork of Shadow, a modern jailbreak detection
bypass by jjolano <https://github.com/jjolano/shadow>.

Upstream copyright: Copyright (c) 2023, jjolano.
Upstream license: BSD 3-Clause (see LICENSE in this repository).

The fork ships under its own product name, Antumbra, and its own package
identifier (me.fedorovskyi.antumbra), and adds hardening for iOS 15-18
jailbreak environments: additional hook lanes, per-app opt-out tooling,
pane-language selection and packaging for rootless Dopamine. Modifications
since the fork point are Copyright (c) 2026, HRYHORII FEDOROVSKYI, and are
distributed under the same BSD 3-Clause license.

This fork is not affiliated with, sponsored by, or endorsed by the original
author. The core's internal identifiers (Shadow.framework, ShadowCore.dylib,
Shadow.dylib, ShadowSettings.bundle and the me.jjolano.shadow prefs domain)
are retained only to stay compatible with existing Shadow installations and
verified injection lanes; they do not imply endorsement.

The distributed Debian package declares Provides/Replaces/Conflicts against
the upstream identifiers so it can replace, but not silently impersonate, the
original package. The About page inside the settings pane credits the core
author separately from the fork maintainer.

The upstream README cites the Copyright Act, RSC 1985, c C-42, s 41.12. That
note is upstream's own and is not a license grant from this fork.
